{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And its meal-offering: two tenths.</b> Our Rabbis, may their memory be blessed, said: this is different from all other lambs, for you will not find a lamb in the Torah whose meal-offering is more than one tenth. But regarding the libation it is not different, as it is written: ״ונסכו יין רביעית ההין״. And therefore we expound at the beginning of the musaf: three tenths for a bull, and two tenths for a ram, and one tenth for a lamb — only because we find a lamb whose meal-offering is different, namely two tenths. But regarding the libation we say only ״ויין כנסכו״ alone, and we do not expound the libations, because we do not find any lamb that is different regarding the wine libation. And therefore it is written ונסכו here with a heh for midrashic exposition — ״ונסכה״ refers back to ״כלה מנחה״. For had it written ונסכו, I would have said it refers back to ״עשרון ועשרון״. And according to the plain sense, it implies that one of the two tenths constitutes the meal-offering of the omer, which is one tenth, and it comes with this lamb, while the second tenth is the tenth appropriate for its meal-offering. And know that its libation is only a quarter-log, as with other libations."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:25.184637106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}